.TH MANAGEDISKS-CLI 1 "2026-10-09" "ManageDisks 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
managedisks-cli \- command line disk and partition manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B managedisks-cli
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B managedisks-cli shell
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scriptable access to everything the ManageDisks window can do. Commands that
change disks must run as root and ask for confirmation unless \fB\-\-yes\fR
is given. \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the exact commands without running them.
.PP
Sizes accept K, M, G, T (binary, e.g. 20G), KB, MB, GB, TB (decimal), sectors
(2048s) and percentages (50%). A bare number means MiB.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Disks, partitions and unallocated space.
.TP
.BI info " device"
Details of a disk or partition.
.TP
.B support
Which filesystems can be created, resized, checked... and which packages
are missing.
.TP
.BI table " disk gpt|mbr"
Create a new, empty partition table (erases the disk).
.TP
.BI create " disk"
Create a partition: \fB\-s\fR size, \fB\-\-start\fR position, \fB\-f\fR
filesystem, \fB\-L\fR label, \fB\-\-name\fR, \fB\-t\fR type,
\fB\-\-encrypt\fR, \fB\-\-logical\fR, \fB\-\-extended\fR.
.TP
.BI delete " partition"
Delete a partition.
.TP
.BI format " partition " \-f " fs"
Format a partition (\fB\-L\fR label, \fB\-\-encrypt\fR).
.TP
.BI resize " partition"
Grow, shrink and/or move: \fB\-\-size\fR 30G, +5G, max or
\fB\-\-size=\-5G\fR; \fB\-\-start\fR or \fB\-\-move\-by=\fR+1G.
.TP
.BI label " partition label"
Set the filesystem label.
.TP
.BI set " partition"
Partition type (\fB\-t\fR), GPT name (\fB\-\-name\fR), GPT attributes
(\fB\-\-attr\fR NAME=on|off) or the MBR boot flag (\fB\-\-boot\fR on|off).
.TP
.BI uuid " partition"
Give the filesystem a new random UUID.
.TP
.BI check " partition"
Check and repair a filesystem (\fB\-\-no\-repair\fR to only report).
.TP
.BI copy " partition disk"
Copy a partition into unallocated space.
.TP
.BI wipe " device"
Erase (\fB\-m\fR quick|zero|random|discard).
.TP
.BI convert " disk gpt|mbr"
Convert the partition table keeping all data.
.TP
.BR mount ", " unmount ", " open ", " close
Mount/unmount filesystems; unlock/lock LUKS volumes.
.TP
.BI smart " disk"
Drive health; \fB\-\-test\fR short|long starts a self-test.
.TP
.BI surface " device"
Read-only scan for unreadable sectors.
.TP
.BR "image create" " device file, " "image restore" " file device"
Save a disk/partition to an image, or write an ISO/IMG (also .xz, .gz,
\&.bz2) to a device.
.TP
.BI clone " source target"
Clone a whole disk.
.TP
.B shell
Interactive console with diskpart-style commands (LIST DISK, SELECT DISK n,
CREATE PARTITION PRIMARY SIZE=n, FORMAT FS=ext4 QUICK, EXTEND, SHRINK,
CLEAN, CONVERT GPT, ASSIGN, ...). Type HELP inside the shell.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo managedisks-cli table /dev/sdb gpt
sudo managedisks-cli create /dev/sdb -s 512M -f fat32 -t esp -L EFI
sudo managedisks-cli create /dev/sdb -f ext4 -L data
sudo managedisks-cli resize /dev/sdb2 --size=-10G
sudo managedisks-cli image restore archlinux.iso /dev/sdc
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on errors, 2 when a surface test found bad sectors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR managedisks (1)
